{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@","kind":"attribute"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","text":"MainActor","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OUDSPinCodeInput"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Layouts","anchor":"Layouts"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The component can be rendered as two different layouts:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"outlined","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" layout: A minimalist input with a transparent background and a visible stroke outlining the field.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"This style may be interesting for contexts other than form pages, e.g. when inputs need to feel lightweight and unobtrusive,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in a header (search field), or in a selection\/filtering feature in a product catalog"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not outlined"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (default): An input with a subtle background fill and visible bottom border, creating a softer and more contained look."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Best suited for dense layouts or to enhance visibility."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The component provides 3 layouts for the input: 4 boxes, 6 boxes or 8 boxes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A helper text can be used to support text to convey additional information about the input field, such as how it will be used."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It should ideally only take up a single line, though may wrap to multiple lines if required, and be either persistently visible or visible only on focus."}]},{"text":"Error status","level":2,"anchor":"Error-status","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Error status indicates that the user input does not meet validation rules or expected formatting."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It provides immediate visual feedback, typically through a red border, error icon, and a clear, accessible error message positioned below the input (mandatory)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"This state helps users quickly identify and correct mistakes by explaining what went wrong and, when possible, how to fix it.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The input remains editable, encouraging users to revise their input without starting over.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The error state must be triggered by an explicit validation (submission, API response), and not in real time with each keystroke.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This can occur either because the entered code does not match the expected code, because the user entered an expired or already used code,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or finally if the maximum number of attempts has been exceeded.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Specific design guidelines","anchor":"Specific-design-guidelines","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In the context of a PIN code input, in addition to the input’s “Error” UI rendering, it is essential to also include an “Alert” component","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(also in its “Error” status) in the interface.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Particular cases","anchor":"Particular-cases"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput"},{"type":"text","text":" component supports autofill feature of values like OTP code."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For example if the user receives a message with inside a code the system can extract, the keyboard can suggest to the user to fill it."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"If the digits fits the component, it will be filled."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"If the digits are longer, they will be truncated."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"If the digits are shorter, they will be filled, letting other fields empty.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The copy\/paste feature is also available and has the same behavior."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Technical-considerations","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Technical considerations"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For some cases, on phones screens or with 8 boxes in iPhone, you may need to use a ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScrollView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to embed the component and let user move it.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["ScrollView(.horizontal) {","    OUDSPinCodeInput($value,","                     length: .eight,","                     helperText: \"Enter your secret code sent to your phone\")","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note also the exposed "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"value"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Binding"},{"type":"text","text":" will be updated when all digits are written."}],"type":"strong"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Accessibility considerations","anchor":"Accessibility-considerations"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The content of the fields is vocalized by Voice Over; the placeholders (defined in "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/obfuscationCharacter"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput\/placeholderCharacter"},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are not vocalized to let users know what they wrote."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The component gets only numeric values, not letters or symbols, only numbers.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Depending on the component configuration, autofocus can still be used when the component appears, and focus is moved to the next field as digits are entered."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For example if Voice Over is enavled, the autoficus is disabled."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The component and its digit fields are vocalized with internal wording."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When using the error status, provide a clear, concise error message explaining what went wrong and, when possible, how to fix it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(for example: "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“The code you entered is invalid. Try again.”"}]},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use helper text to communicate additional guidance (for example: ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“Check the 6‑digit code sent by SMS”"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"), and keep this text short so it remains easy to vocalize"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and understand."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Rich-text","text":"Rich text","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Rich text can be used for error and helper texts."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Strong text can be used sparingly to highlight key information within the content.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"No other text styles should be used.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Underlined text must not be applied manually (e.g. in error message), as it is commonly associated with hyperlinks and may mislead users.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Code-samples","text":"Code samples","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["    \/\/ The value with the code","    @State private var pinCode: String = \"\"","","    \/\/ By default, the PIN code input displays only 6 boxes","    OUDSPinCodeInput($pinCode)","","    \/\/ It can have also up 4 or 8 boxes, with an helper text","    OUDSPinCodeInput($pinCode, length: .eight, helperText: \"Enter your 8 secret digits\")","","    \/\/ The component can be used in error contexts","    OUDSPinCodeInput($pinCode, length: .six, status: .error(message: \"The OTP code you entered is not correct\"))"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Design-documentation","text":"Design documentation","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/r.orange.fr\/r\/S-ouds-doc-pin-code-input"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Themes-rendering","text":"Themes rendering","type":"heading"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Orange","text":"Orange","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"component_pinCodeInput_Orange","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Orange Compact","anchor":"Orange-Compact","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"component_pinCodeInput_OrangeCompact"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Sosh","anchor":"Sosh","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"component_pinCodeInput_Sosh"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Wireframe","anchor":"Wireframe","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"component_pinCodeInput_Wireframe","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","name":"Version","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"1.3.0 (Figma component design version)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"},{"type":"aside","name":"Since","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"1.4.0","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/oudscomponents\/oudspincodeinput"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSPinCodeInput","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14OUDSComponents16OUDSPinCodeInputV","roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OUDSPinCodeInput","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"Components"}],"title":"OUDSPinCodeInput","symbolKind":"struct","platforms":[{"beta":false,"introducedAt":"15.0","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"name":"iOS"},{"beta":false,"introducedAt":"1.0","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"name":"visionOS"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"OUDSPinCodeInput"}]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"PIN code input is a UI element that allows to capture short, fixed-length numeric codes, typically for authentication or confirmation purposes,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"such as a four, six or eight-digit personal identification number (PIN).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"PIN code input is presented as a series of individual input fields or boxes, each representing a single digit, to enhance readability and encourage accurate input,"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"while supporting smooth keyboard navigation and secured input masking if needed.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"topicSec